{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1562811-w20-kinfolk-idea-empathic-healers-dangerous-convalesence","id":1562811,"title":"W20 Kinfolk Idea Empathic healers dangerous Convalesence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-06T19:59:36-07:00","id":1562811,"title":"W20 Kinfolk Idea Empathic healers dangerous Convalesence","content":"My idea is some Garou Kin with Empathic healing cures a narcisst or sociopath who wsas sexual;ly violent and or a murderer.<br /> <br /> <br /> It will take them months to recover <br /> <br /> ideas how they can be confined?<br /> <br /> OOne idea is former Narcissit or whateevver acting as his Saviors warden","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T23:04:59-07:00","id":1562817,"title":"","content":"Narcissism and Sociopathy don't cause violent behavior, regardless of not controlling it. Most of those patients are nonviolent despite being terrible in their relationships in one way or another, and some are even ok people.<br /> <br /> Do not, ever, equate mental health problems and conditions with crime and violence. This is pure, despicable prejudice that perpetuates a series of violence cycles where those people and many others are victims, not perpetrators.<br /> <br /> Your kinfolk would acquire a mental condition, what we call a Personality Disorder, but the actual result would come from who they are filtered through the disorder, Instead of copying stupid stereotypes try to look for the actual symptoms in sites like the Mayo Clinic, Harvard and even Wikipedia, read at least two or three reputable medical sites. This will give you an actual idea of what is this filter the healer will go through.<br /> <br /> And I don't think they'd let the former bastard be their keeper. What's even the point? But the specific result will weight a lot on what has or can actually be done, from tying them and leaving a Garou bodyguard to just having them live with a roommate with some prepare to deal with their condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T23:46:14-07:00","id":1562818,"title":"","content":"From a more game-play oriented perspective:<br /> <br /> 1) Since Empathic Healing is kind of a shit power for PCs because it can effectively remove them from play for such prolonged periods of time as it is (and even mental trauma isn't that hard to heal in WtA through other supernatural means), it's probably best to read what it can do in the least penalizing way so players might actually use it; or seek out NPCs with it. I would treat that phrase &quot;state of psychosis&quot; has imparting the disorder but not necessarily the specific manifestations of the individual healed. So an Empathic Healer can cure someone's narcissism at the cost of becoming a clinical narcissist, but their narcissism is going to manifest in a way that makes sense for the healer's own mental state and history rather than copying the patient's specifics.<br /> <br /> 2) However interesting it might be to contemplate certain hypotheticals as thought exercises, for actual use in game it's worth being very careful with putting PCs in a position to foist an intense violent urge on either themselves or someone else that could easily get very hard to handle for the players. I think it would be an absolute minimum t ensure that everyone at the table is comfortable with RP going in that direction, and that at least OOC if it's going to happen it should be extremely clear what's about to happen before anything gets committed to IC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T05:58:50-07:00","id":1562827,"title":"","content":"Another overlapping RP/RL issue is where to define the line of what's healable and what's not from the nature of the condition.<br /> <br /> How Empathic Healing treats a mutilation vs an amputation vs an inborn lack of a limb vs a genetic lack of a limb? Those can be superficially similar, but are extremely different both biologically and metaphysically. Mage would ask the nature of the Pattern, and have very different implications for each one.<br /> <br /> Mental conditions aren't less complex, they're maybe even more, but in a less obvious way. The reason Narcissism and Antisocial are in a group called Personality Disorders is that they affect fundamental personality traits at the core, to the point where it's legitimately questionable if a &quot;cured&quot; person can be considered the same person at all. They're born like that, there's some genetic factor, the difference is present from birth and resistant to changes in environment or parental style.<br /> <br /> So... Is this a disease? If so, how much of it? Not every aspect necessarily has the same answer. Neurodevelopmental disorders like Autism, Hyperactivity and Down Syndrome have symptoms that can be controlled with intervention, but others come from biological format and configuration of the brain and are not just currently without cure, but probably beyond cure on a conceptual level.<br /> <br /> Those are politically loaded questions, so you shouldn't answer out of feelings alone, but they are also loaded in emotional intensity for one's group, metaphysically loaded for the setting and mechanically loaded for the game.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't mean, actually, that they're too hard to answer or too rigid, they can be fun to work with and generate a plethora of options. But does mean it can't be a sloppy, lazy work, or you'll end up with problems you don't want (rather than problems you do)<br /> <br /> Finally, it's important to remember that your decisions as ST are not known to the character, not even the NPC Healer. They may believe any bullshit before trying and formulate any other explanation for what actually happened after. Your idea of they getting the sexual violence tendencies is horrible as the actual fact that'll transpire, <i><b>but is perfectly fine as what they are thinking will happen</b></i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T10:23:08-07:00","id":1562836,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure they're that mechanically loaded once you've gotten past the other considerations. If you've already run through all the other considerations and come to the conclusion for your table that someone born with one arm doesn't have anything to &quot;heal&quot; mechanically and can only have a second arm via supernatural means that would also let a two-armed person have a third arm (or more likely four arms because bilateral symmetry is more likely to be pursued), then it's relatively easy to sort through which powers can't do anything about it and which can.<br /> <br /> While it might not be as clear in WtA (again, just talking about the mechanics) because generally speaking WtA doesn't focus on that level of mind or body alteration mechanics, you can at least look to games like Mage for ideas of what's &quot;normal&quot; in the family of games for these concepts; as Mage definitely does address these sorts of questions because it comes up far more readily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T20:51:03-07:00","id":1562862,"title":"","content":"Oh, I agree. I was more exploring nuance to give ideas and being my usual verbose self.<br /> <br /> As long as the questions are there, the process should go smoothly. The important part is just to not be lazy and end up in a tight spot later.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking, now from what I know of those conditions, some ways I could run it:<br /> <br /> The ritual seems to have succeeded and they part ways. Those who guard the Healer will stay nearby and will notice narcissistic behavior as expected. With time they get wind of the news that the healed actually remains the same. Then that time is passing and the Healer isn't improving. Those who lived with the Healer are overall happier, and when they visit they don't notice anything abnormal, the Healer is exactly the same as always for them. The Empathic Healer was already narcissistic. This is well within their ballpark and others wouldn't have noticed. The ritual failed, impossible to say if it's because it can't be done or because the Healer can't be doubly narcissistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T16:03:25-07:00","id":1563651,"title":"","content":"Ideas what to do with former asshole as the healer sacrafived themselves to grant them lucidity so you cant send them to prison","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T20:49:30-07:00","id":1563666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1562811-w20-kinfolk-idea-empathic-healers-dangerous-convalesence?p=1563651#post1563651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas what to do with former asshole as the healer sacrafived themselves to grant them lucidity so you cant send them to prison</div> </div> </div> </div>Drop the whole idea.<br /> <br /> The problem is you wanting to magically &quot;cure assholery&quot; as a straightforward concept.<br /> <br /> Making someone change their mind through a spell of any sort is called brainwashing, and it's generally and with good reason frowned upon.<br /> <br /> It's extremely rare for mental illness of any sort to cause criminal behavior, popular depiction of conditions like psychopathy are greatly out of synch with reality. When those people do commit crimes, more often than not it has little to do with their mental condition. They should go to jail.<br /> <br /> When a mental illness does cause someone to commit crimes in a way they couldn't resist or understand, that's called in US criminal insanity and is grounds to go to therapy rather than jail, so problem solved.<br /> <br /> But a problem here is you insisting in defining asshole = mental illness. You don't want to explore how illness can cause someone to do bad things, you want to equate being bad with having a mental condition. This is prejudice of the kind that still to this day is used to justify a lot of social and institutional violence against all sorts of people, and the kind of argument that proponents of Conversion Therapy use to legitimate victimization of minorities through supposedly healing processes.<br /> <br /> Stop this. Stop trying to say a character was bad because they were ill and now became a better person because they got healed of their evil. Stop vilifying illness and promoting the idea of conformity as &quot;cure&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}